  "notes": {
    "h1": "R6A-H1: rows joined on pr_number (self-hosted joint v3 test \u2229 hosted run-5 v3 test, non-error); an answer agrees when both probabilities are on the same side of 0.5 (>= 0.5 = yes). \u0394p = self-hosted \u2212 hosted. Not used to tune anything (R6A.4).",
    "h3": "R6A-H3: run5._h5_model unchanged \u2014 isotonic (out_of_bounds=clip) fitted on the self-hosted val answers vs `iterated`, applied to the self-hosted test answers. If no self-hosted val rows exist, the raw answer's AUC is reported and marked 'val not run'. Pair AUC: run-4 R4-H2 test pairs (kind != retrieved, or retrieved with a_label = superseded_by), duplicate_of = P(same) + 0.5 P(subset); needs results/run4/pairs.jsonl for the pair kinds. If R6A-H1 fails the row is 'a different model': H3 is reported, not compared.",
    "h4": "R6A-H4: single = one request per question (predict --single-question; 10 sequential calls per PR, latency = wall-clock of the PR). Compared on the PRs answered in both modes. Calibrated AUCs when both modes have their own val rows (each refit on its own val answers), otherwise raw AUCs for both (isotonic is monotone, so raw ranks \u2248 calibrated ranks); which one is stated as `basis`.",
    "h2": "R6A-H2: open-loop replay (cli loadtest, v3, joint, 600 test PRs, 429 retry off) from the gate client on the same VM (loopback). Bar = R3-H5: \u00d7100 p99 <= \u00d71 p99 + 200 ms and 0 errors. Saturation = first multiplier in 1,10,30,100,300 whose p99 exceeds 2 \u00d7 the \u00d71 p99. Load-test p99 is per decision (one joint request).",
    "cost": "Cost: $/1k PRs = usd_per_hour (serve_meta.json) / (rate_per_s \u00d7 3600 / 1000) at the highest multiplier with 0 errors (PROTOCOL R6A.3). Hosted: run-5 in-run mean list-price cost per PR \u00d7 1000."
  },
